:: StoryTitle
The Lantern Keeper

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "5B7F3C52-8E0D-4A4B-9C55-0F1D6F2A9E11",
  "format": "Twee3",
  "start": "Start"
}

:: Start
Fog rolls over the cliffs. A dark lighthouse stands at the end of the path, its door ajar and a light in one window.

[[Climb the spiral stairs->Stairs]]
[[Check the cellar->Cellar]]
[[Knock at the keeper's door->Keeper]]

:: Stairs
The stairs wind up into the dark. Halfway, there is a landing with a wooden bench, and above it a hatch to the lamp room.

[[Open the hatch->Lamp]]
[[Rest on the bench->Landing]]

:: Cellar
The cellar smells of oil and salt. On a shelf sits an old brass lantern, still warm. A stair leads back up.

[[Take the lantern->Lantern]]
[[Go back up->Stairs]]

:: Keeper
An old keeper opens the door before you knock. "You are late," he says, and holds out a steaming cup.

[[Accept the tea->Tea]]

:: Lamp
The great lamp is cold. Its glass is clouded, and far out at sea a ship sounds its horn.

[[Light the lamp->Beacon]]
[[Leave it dark->Dark]]

:: Landing
The bench is warm from the day. Fog presses against the window, and you are very tired.

[[Sleep->Sleep]]

:: Lantern
The lantern hums in your hand and casts a steady yellow glow. It would light the lamp in an instant.

[[Carry it up to the lamp->Lamp]]

:: Tea
The tea tastes of smoke and honey. The keeper smiles, hands you his keys, and walks out into the fog. The lighthouse is yours now.

:: Beacon
The lamp catches. A beam sweeps the water and the ship turns away from the rocks. At dawn the crew rows in to thank you.

:: Dark
Without your light the ship finds the rocks. You watch the fog swallow the sound, and the lighthouse stays dark.

:: Sleep
You wake at noon. The fog is gone, the lamp is unlit, and the keeper never returns. Some stories are only a nap.
